## Project contract changes

### Version control

```markdown
## Version control

Never develop directly on `main`, `master`, `develop`, or `default`. Create each
task branch from an up-to-date `develop` using `feature/<short-slug>` and use it for
the whole task.

Run the relevant checks before committing. Commit every coherent, independently
verifiable increment instead of accumulating the whole task in one commit. Use
`<type>: <what changed and why>` with `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, or
`chore`. Reference an issue or specification when one exists, but neither is
required.

End every agent-authored commit body with a blank line followed by
`Assisted-by: <harness>/<model>/<effort>`.

The final verified result is one full Git object ID. Any subsequent commit
invalidates its review and verification gates.
```

The `<short-slug>` here is the executor-chosen Git branch slug. It is not the topology slug.

### Backlog

`docs/backlog.md` contains only unfinished, deferred, blocked, knowingly unfixed, or unsupported work. Completed entries are deleted. Git is completion history.

### Documentation

Update existing knowledge only when made new or false. Do not create changelogs, migration notes, reports, per-directory READMEs, or cleanup narratives without an explicit requirement or named durable consumer.

Update existing full-turn-retrieval and distribution decisions rather than creating narration documents.

Append original request and clarifications verbatim to `docs/business.md`.

