### Decomposition Readiness

Items 1–5 and most of item 7 are now reasonably assignable without new architectural decisions.

Item 6 still requires the implementer to invent:

- wrapper grammar;
- multi-batch buffering;
- release semantics;
- adjudication exchange batching;
- exact extraction command fields;
- the literal Node recipe.

Those should be specified before decomposition.

### Weak-Model Executability

A weaker model could implement topology, lifecycle waiting, catalogue bundling, header matrices, candidate checks, retry guards, glossary reconciliation, and most acceptance tests.

It would still have to guess at:

- the exact relay wrapper;
- how the executor behaves between batches;
