7. executor/E2E single-batch V1 fail-closed behavior;
8. sequential independent A/B and mutation barrier;
9. mutating reviewer check preserves completed `checks=FAIL` result; unexplained dirt discards affected output;
10. reviewer-owned QC/smoke/check interpretation;
11. byte-identical adversarial wrapper transport;
12. NUL, UTF-8, newline, delimiter injection, and ambiguous delivery behavior;
13. finding closure/adjudication/invalidation accounting;
14. same-SHA lifecycle completion;
15. commit invalidation;
16. restart as new sessions;
17. bundled live catalogue isolation and separate launchability;
18. no ordinary menus or manual Enter;
19. instrumented tracked-content firewall with canary;
20. controlled scratch deletion, lost-scratch failure, and no cross-run scan;
